Third-party and lineage notes
-----------------------------

Task designs and assets
  HandsOn incorporates selected task designs and assets from DexJoCo
  (https://github.com/brave-eai/dexjoco) and DexVerse
  (https://github.com/ycyao216/DexVerse).  Per-task
  attribution, including which tasks reuse an upstream asset family, is given
  in the task-inventory appendix of the HandsOn manuscript.  The upstream
  projects are distributed under their own licenses; consult them directly.

Historical asset names
  Some locally authored assets retain a dexverse_authored prefix in
  development source bundles, while several preliminary DexVerse assets
  were replaced before data collection.  Attribution follows documented
  task-design adaptations and retained asset reuse, rather than historical
  directory names or candidates considered during development.

Simulator
  Simulation and data collection use NVIDIA Isaac Sim / Isaac Lab, which are
  distributed under the NVIDIA Software License Agreement.

Vendored assets
  Task assets carry their own licenses next to the asset, e.g.
  taskdev/tasks/*/assets/*/LICENSE.txt.  These include CC BY and CC0 works
  whose attribution requirements are stated in those files.

OpenPI
  The openpi/ directory is derived from OpenPI and is distributed under the
  Apache License 2.0; see openpi/LICENSE and openpi/NOTICE.  Gemma-based model
  components are additionally subject to the Gemma Terms of Use
  (openpi/LICENSE_GEMMA.txt).

Reference clients
  docs/reference_code/ contains integration examples for third-party policy
  stacks.  docs/reference_code/handson_lerobot_client/ adapts the LeRobot robot
  and asynchronous-inference interfaces (Apache License 2.0), and
  docs/reference_code/handson_dp_eval/ follows the Diffusion Policy evaluation
  structure (MIT).  Both are adapted against their upstream interfaces rather
  than vendored; install the upstream packages from their own releases and
  consult their licenses directly.  Neither upstream is redistributed here.

Robot descriptions
  Third-party arm and hand descriptions retain their own licenses and notices.
  Exact models, pinned source repositories, modifications and known provenance
  gaps are documented in docs/robot-assets.md and per-model SOURCE.json files
  under handson/handson/assets/robots/. Citation entries are in
  docs/robot-assets.bib. These assets are not relicensed by the repository MIT
  license.

  ROKAE AR5-08 meshes match rokae_description 0.0.5 in the public Airomantic/ar3_ws
  mirror, pinned in SOURCE.json. That package explicitly declares Apache-2.0.
  Its declaration, full license text, mesh correspondence and benchmark
  parameter adaptations accompany the bundled descriptions and converted layers.
  The mirror is not represented as an official manufacturer-hosted release.
  Legacy AR5-07 meshes have separate official Apache-2.0 provenance.

  Tianji M6-CCS source files and generated URDFs are not redistributed while
  the exact BSD variant/text remain unresolved. Local import instructions and
  pinned upstream links are in docs/robot-assets.md; links grant no extra rights.
